#    the durable record of the pin, not that file)
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODEL ARTIFACT (GGUF file digest + quantization)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   file:   /mnt/data1/models/Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.3.Q4_K_M.gguf
#   sha256: f5074b1221da0f5a2910d33b642efa5b9eb58cfdddca1c79e16d7ad28aa2b31f
#   bytes:  4372811712
#   quant:  Q4_K_M          params: 7.2B          arch: llama
#   gguf:   general.name = "Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.3"  (v3, 291 tensors, 25 kv)
#
#   PROVENANCE — this is the SAME ARTIFACT the 2026-07-13 ollama positive
#   control ran on, not merely the same build. ollama stores the model layer of
#   mistral:latest as the raw GGUF and names blobs by their SHA-256; this file
#   was staged byte-for-byte from that blob, and its recomputed digest matches
#   the blob name exactly. Model weights are therefore removed as a variable in
#   the container-vs-control comparison.
#     ollama manifest: registry.ollama.ai/library/mistral/latest
#     model layer:     sha256:f5074b1221da0f5a2910d33b642efa5b9eb58cfdddca1c79e16d7ad28aa2b31f
#     ollama tag digest (NOT the artifact digest): 6577803aa9a036369e481d648a2baebb381ebc6e897f2bb9a766a2aa7bfbc1cf
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SAMPLING REGIME
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   temperature: 0.8       seeds: [1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8] (run N uses seeds[N-1])
#   max_tokens:  512       thinking-mode: N/A (Mistral-7B-v0.3 has no thinking mode)
#
#   NOT pinned separately — declared inside study.toml, so it is covered
#   transitively by the study.toml digest below and by the runtime StudyDigest
#   over the derived study.json. That placement is deliberate: while sampling
#   was a Go constant it was pinned only by the runner build, which the freeze
#   rule does not accept. See CHANGELOG.md v2.
